--
symbol 'read' is unknown
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/1, [temp.point]: a class template specialization is completed
only from a *definition* of the template.  CBMC eagerly elaborates a
specialization referenced while the template is only forward-declared, producing
an empty-but-complete class that masks members added by the later definition
("symbol 'read' is unknown").  Reduced (cvise, from preprocessed <istream>) form
of the lispexpr.cpp / parser.cpp dog-food failures (<iosfwd> forward-declares
std::basic_istream before <istream> defines it).  A fix must defer instantiation
until the template is defined without mis-firing on partial-specialization-
defined templates (std::function) or leaving library types incomplete (the
std::ostringstream layout invariant).  Flip to CORE once fixed.
